1
00:00:00,970 --> 00:00:03,290
Your computer has never
seen a single photo.

2
00:00:03,290 --> 00:00:07,090
Not even the ones it
shows you every day.

3
00:00:07,770 --> 00:00:11,210
All it does is shuffle
patterns of on and off, very,

4
00:00:11,450 --> 00:00:12,250
very fast.

5
00:00:12,930 --> 00:00:15,390
When you open a photo,
the chip isn't looking at

6
00:00:15,390 --> 00:00:16,190
a face.

7
00:00:16,670 --> 00:00:19,550
It's moving numbers that
say how bright each tiny

8
00:00:19,550 --> 00:00:21,410
dot on your screen should be.

9
00:00:22,130 --> 00:00:24,710
When you play a song,
it's sending numbers to

10
00:00:24,710 --> 00:00:25,510
a speaker.

11
00:00:25,990 --> 00:00:29,330
The switches don't know
what a face is, or a song,

12
00:00:29,890 --> 00:00:30,690
or a joke.

13
00:00:31,190 --> 00:00:31,990
They just flip.

14
00:00:32,710 --> 00:00:34,050
So where does the
meaning come from?

15
00:00:34,830 --> 00:00:37,150
It only happens when
the pattern reaches you.

16
00:00:37,870 --> 00:00:40,190
All the meaning is on
your side of the screen.
